# CITATION.cff

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, research protocol, or audit record, please cite this repository release and its Zenodo DOI."
title: "CE-1 Continuous Existence: Episodic Memory Instrument, Research Audit, and Experiment Redesign"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
abstract: >
  CE-1 Continuous Existence is a research software and experimental-protocol
  repository investigating episodic memory, continuity-related behavior, and the
  distinction between retrieval of stored information and subjective experience in
  AI systems. The repository includes the episodic-memory implementation, research
  protocols, experiment runners, validation tools, research artifacts, audit reports,
  and a corrected redesign of the initial experiments. The initial experiments do
  not establish that retrieved episodes causally influence cognition. H1 and H2
  are classified as inconclusive. No claim about consciousness, phenomenal
  experience, or personal identity is made.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - episodic memory
  - machine memory
  - cognitive architecture
  - continuity
  - reproducible research
  - research software
  - experiment design
  - computational consciousness
  - causal inference
  - in-context learning
  - auditability
authors:
  - name: "CE-1 Research Programme"
    affiliation: "Independent research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ce-1-continuous-existence/ce-1-continuous-existence"
